            "review_title": "Review at V-Smile",
            "review_text": "Veronica M\nMarfa, Texas7 contributions\n0\nQuaint restaurant, lovely owners, great value\nMay 2015 • Business\nWe stayed at one of the big hotels on the strip, which was great, but the breakfast was way overpriced so we looked for something close by that gave us more for our money. We stumbled upon V-Smile and loved it at first sight--so much so that we proceeded to eat there for the next two mornings, same order each day. Omelets, vietnamese coffee, and watermelon juice. They cook up a great basic meal, the coffee is very tasty (not a given in Nha Trang), and the value can't be beat. Plus, the owners are super friendly. One of the women told us that her parents live in the U.S., in North Carolina, so that was something to bond over; we snapped a photo with her on our last morning there, and it felt bittersweet to depart :( Definitely worth eating there if you're in Nha Trang, where a lot of the restaurants are hit or miss.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 28, 2015",
